Recommends: gnome-keyring
Description: Tokkl timer service for the GNOME Shell extension
 A session bus service for Tokkl, a self-hosted time tracker with a Toggl
 Track compatible API. It signs in to an account on a Tokkl server, keeps the
 running timer, starts and stops it, and sets the project and billable flag
 of the next or running entry. The Tokkl GNOME Shell extension shows it in
 the top bar.
 .
 It owns org.tokkl.Timer1 and starts on the first call to that name, through
 its systemd user unit or D-Bus activation. The token or password is stored
 in the keyring through libsecret. Built for Debian 13 amd64 with Qt 6.8.
